    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1030">

                <pb facs="1198" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–1845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1030<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Political Adviser to the Representative on the European Advisory
                        Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mosely</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1030-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-18">18 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tripartite Conference Babelsberg for Mosely from Winant serial number 4307.</p>
                <p>… No word to date received at Soviet Embassy here from Moscow permitting
                    clearance and signature of … agreement amending agreement on zones Germany.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
